.TH BEASTIE 1 "2026-11-14" "Beastie 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
beastie \- RedhotBSD terminal emulator
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B beastie
.RB [ \-\-version ]
.RB [ \-\-selftest ]
.RI [ st-options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B beastie
is a wrapper around
.BR st (1),
the suckless terminal emulator.
.PP
On launch, the wrapper exports
.BR TERM=beastie-256color ,
sets a default font of
.BR "Iosevka Term:size=13" ,
a default geometry of
.BR 100x30 ,
and a window title of
.BR Beastie .
Any remaining arguments are passed to
.BR st ,
so the flags documented in
.BR st (1)
work unchanged, and an explicit
.B \-t
overrides the default title.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the Beastie version and exit. The output is
.BR "beastie 1.0.0 (st 0.9.3)" .
.TP
.B \-\-selftest
Check that
.B st
is in
.BR PATH
and that the
.B beastie-256color
terminfo entry is registered. Exit code is 0 on success and 1 on failure.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B TERM
Set to
.B beastie-256color
by the wrapper. The entry must exist in the terminfo database, which the
installer places at
.B $HOME/.terminfo
on Linux and
.B /usr/local/share/misc
on FreeBSD.
.TP
.B DISPLAY
The X11 display to connect to. Required.
.TP
.B TERMINFO
Optional. If set, overrides the default terminfo search path.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B $HOME/.Xresources
Holds the four
.B st
properties the installer manages:
.BR st.background ,
.BR st.foreground ,
.BR st.cursorColor ,
and
.BR st.font .
Edit the file, run
.BR "xrdb -merge ~/.Xresources" ,
and restart
.B beastie
to apply.
.TP
.B /usr/local/bin/beastie
The wrapper script.
.TP
.B /usr/local/bin/st
The compiled terminal binary.
.TP
.B $HOME/.terminfo/b/beastie-256color
The terminfo entry on Linux.
.TP
.B /usr/local/share/misc/terminfo.db
The terminfo entry on FreeBSD.
.SH KEYBINDINGS
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+C
Copy the current selection to the X11
.B CLIPBOARD
selection.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+V
Paste from the X11
.B CLIPBOARD
selection.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+N
Open a new
.B beastie
window.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+D
Run
.B "devil ."
in the current directory. Requires
.B devil
in
.BR PATH .
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+F
Run
.B "nid ."
in the current directory. Requires
.B nid
in
.BR PATH .
.TP
.B Shift+PgUp
Scroll back through the 5,000 line history.
.TP
.B Shift+PgDn
Scroll forward.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success. Applies only to
.B \-\-version
and
.BR \-\-selftest .
A normal launch inherits
.BR st 's
exit status.
.TP
.B 1
Failure in
.BR \-\-selftest ,
either because
.B st
is not in
.B PATH
or because the terminfo entry is missing.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR st (1),
.BR xrdb (1),
.BR X (7)
.SH BUGS
.B Ctrl+Shift+Q
is not implemented in V1.0. Use the window manager close action instead.
.PP
The
.B alpha
patch requires a running compositor. Without one the background is opaque,
regardless of the
.B alpha
value in
.BR config.h .
.PP
Report bugs at the project repository.
.SH AUTHOR
RedhotBSD project.